{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01311",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.86,
      "end_seconds": 6.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.0,
      "end_seconds": 10.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.99,
      "end_seconds": 16.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Doctor, um, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.0,
      "end_seconds": 21.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 22.46,
      "end_seconds": 28.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Doctor, it's more breathless than usual. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.25,
      "end_seconds": 31.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.23,
      "end_seconds": 39.08,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "About four days, I think... sorry, five days, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.89,
      "end_seconds": 48.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.59,
      "end_seconds": 68.97,
      "duration_seconds": 18.38,
      "text": "About a five out of ten. It just comes and goes. Yes, walking. That makes it worse. And there's more sputum, a bit yellow as well, about a week now. There was a wheeze, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.62,
      "end_seconds": 73.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.27,
      "end_seconds": 78.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Oh, no allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.71,
      "end_seconds": 82.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.44,
      "end_seconds": 93.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "It's Tiotropium inhaler, once a day. Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 94.52,
      "end_seconds": 101.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it when needed, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.92,
      "end_seconds": 123.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.87,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Oh, uh, I have COPD, for nearly five years. I've got eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.85,
      "end_seconds": 140.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Right, right. Okay, I can see COPD in your file as well. What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.75,
      "end_seconds": 144.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.51,
      "end_seconds": 146.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.95,
      "end_seconds": 150.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.97,
      "end_seconds": 158.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Have you had coughing up blood, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.76,
      "end_seconds": 163.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Not that I've noticed, no coughing up blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.59,
      "end_seconds": 169.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Okay, have you had any chest pain, fever or swollen ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.83,
      "end_seconds": 176.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "I haven't had chest pain, fever or swollen ankles, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.53,
      "end_seconds": 180.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.23,
      "end_seconds": 184.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "No, um, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 203.54,
      "end_seconds": 213.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. SpO2 92 percent on room air, respiratory rate 22, temperature is 37.5 degrees, pulse 100, pressure 140 over 87."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.7,
      "end_seconds": 215.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.92,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.51,
      "end_seconds": 221.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.65,
      "end_seconds": 224.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.95,
      "end_seconds": 242.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "There is wheeze at both bases and your oxygen is a little low."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.16,
      "end_seconds": 258.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.84,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Let me tell you where I've got to. My working impression is a flare-up of COPD. Another possibility is a chest infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.68,
      "end_seconds": 265.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "So, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.8,
      "end_seconds": 279.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.4,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a flare-up of COPD, and we'll know more once the a sputum sample is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.69,
      "end_seconds": 320.99,
      "duration_seconds": 26.3,
      "text": "A sputum sample is what I'd like next, for purulent sputum. Let's get a chest X-ray, for COPD flare. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. What I'm giving you is doxycycline, 100 milligrams, once a day, five days. It's for chest infection. I'm prescribing prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, five days. It's for COPD flare."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.8,
      "end_seconds": 325.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Fine, um, I'll begin it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.68,
      "end_seconds": 338.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "Use your inhaler regularly and get seen if you are not better in three days. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.02,
      "end_seconds": 345.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "Right, right. We'll catch up in one week. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.67,
      "end_seconds": 351.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Good, um, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}